---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { pikobuyRegisterUrl } from '../lib/findspreadsheet';
---
<BaseLayout title="PikoBuy Spreadsheet | Finds, QC Photos & Buying Guide" description="Search PikoBuy-ready product finds from FindSpreadsheet, understand QC photos, and follow a clear buying-agent workflow.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT PRODUCT DISCOVERY</p>
    <h1>PikoBuy Spreadsheet</h1>
    <p class="lede">A searchable path to product finds, source photos and QC research—built around FindSpreadsheet data, then ready to open on PikoBuy.</p>
    <form class="search" action="/search" method="get">
      <label class="sr-only" for="q">Search FindSpreadsheet</label>
      <input id="q" name="q" placeholder="Search shoes, outerwear, bags, electronics…" required />
      <button type="submit">Search finds</button>
    </form>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/finds">Browse data source</a><a class="button" href={pikobuyRegisterUrl()} rel="nofollow sponsored">Create PikoBuy account</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-grid" aria-label="Start here">
    <a href="/finds"><strong>Searchable finds</strong><span>Use the FindSpreadsheet source catalogue instead of an unmaintained copied sheet.</span></a>
    <a href="/guides#qc"><strong>QC photos</strong><span>Learn what warehouse inspection images can and cannot confirm.</span></a>
    <a href="/guides#shipping"><strong>Shipping workflow</strong><span>Understand the two payments, parcel submission and tracking sequence.</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="article">
    <p class="eyebrow">WHAT PEOPLE ACTUALLY SEARCH FOR</p>
    <h2>More than a list of links</h2>
    <p>The useful intent behind a <em>PikoBuy spreadsheet</em> is usually very specific: a visitor wants to locate a product, see the source listing and photos, compare options, then decide whether to use a buying agent. Current search pages compete on the same practical questions—PikoBuy finds, QC photos, Taobao, Weidian, 1688, shipping and how to order. This site is planned around those questions rather than around thin category pages.</p>
    <p>PikoBuy’s public guide describes a sequence of selecting an item or pasting a source link, choosing size and colour, making the initial payment, reviewing warehouse inspection photos, then submitting an international parcel and paying shipping. That means product pages must eventually show the original listing context and QC evidence from the shared source—not invented descriptions or copied prices.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="article muted">
    <h2>SEO roadmap</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Core:</strong> PikoBuy spreadsheet, PikoBuy finds, PikoBuy links.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> PikoBuy QC photos, warehouse inspection, QC checker.</li>
      <li><strong>Source intent:</strong> PikoBuy Taobao, Weidian, 1688 and Yupoo.</li>
      <li><strong>Decision intent:</strong> PikoBuy shipping, how to order, tracking and reviews.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each future article should answer one decision task with sources and update dates. It should never make claims about authenticity, customs outcomes, live stock, delivery times or fees without current evidence.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
